{
  "description": "Golden set for the meal text analysis (Epic 1.9). Each case is what a patient types in the meal form (description, optional portion) and the items a person reading it would expect: food_id from codebase/models/agents/tools/nutrition_data/vn_foods.csv, or null when the food is not in the table (the pipeline must then leave carbs unknown, not guess). quantity/unit are what the patient said; null quantity means none was given and the table's default serving applies. Expected carbs are computed by the eval from these labels through the same table, so the eval measures splitting/matching/portion errors, not the accuracy of the table's numbers (that is the separate cross-check against the Vietnamese food composition table).",
  "tags": {
    "co_dau": "typed with diacritics",
    "khong_dau": "typed without diacritics",
    "viet_tat": "abbreviation (cf, ts, bm...)",
    "nhieu_mon": "several foods in one entry",
    "khau_phan": "amount in the separate portion field",
    "khoi_luong": "mass unit (g, lạng)",
    "mon_la": "contains a food the table does not have",
    "van_noi": "conversational wording around the food list"
  },
